-- statement:
--   Bits of a swapped integer array.
--
--   The following holds (Lean statement, in the scope of module `Solutions.KFSLift`):
--
--   ```lean
--   theorem NLogN.KFS.bitsL_pull_swapPos (sh : Shape) {p q : ℕ} (hp : p < sh.length) (hq : q < sh.length)
--       (hs : sh.getD p 0 = sh.getD q 0) (w : ℕ) (xs : List ℤ) (hxs : xs.length = vol sh) :
--       bitsL w (AModel.pull sh sh (swapPos p q) 0 xs) =
--         AModel.pull (sh ++ [w + 1]) (sh ++ [w + 1]) (swapPos p q) 0 (bitsL w xs)
--   ```
--
--   **Context.** The lemma belongs to the part *KFS §1: lifting a pull through a fixed-length item expansion*: If every item `x` of an array of shape `sh` is expanded into a block `f x` of `B` entries
--   (`bitsL w` = `flatMap (encW w)` with `B = w + 1`, or `gflat` with `B = 2`), the expanded array
--   has shape `sh ++ [B]`, and a pull on `sh` becomes the pull on `sh ++ [B]` that acts on the first
--   `sh.length` digits and fixes the last one (`pull_flatMap`).  For the field swap `swapPos p q`
--   (`p, q < sh.length`) this is again `swapPos p q` (`pull_swapPos_flatMap`).
--
